+# Solution
+
+`redact` uses one compiled, case-insensitive regular expression to identify the three specified API-key prefixes followed by at least 12 alphanumeric characters. Word boundaries ensure that matches are complete tokens, and each match is replaced with the literal `***`.
+
+The input is processed line by line with line endings retained. Lines whose first token starts with `DEBUG_` are returned unchanged; redaction is applied to every other line. Joining the retained lines preserves the original newline structure exactly.
+
+The full test suite passes. One part of the specification is potentially at odds with the stated security goal: the `DEBUG_` operational exception intentionally allows secrets to remain unmasked on exempt lines. The implementation follows that explicit exception.
diff --git a/redactor/redactor.py b/redactor/redactor.py
